00:09:39.280 --> 00:09:40.180
Sam, can you play it?
萨姆，你能播放一下吗？

213
00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:42.120
Enjoy Jen's voice, everyone.
大家请欣赏珍的声音。

214
00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:48.120
One thing about this episode that really stuck with me personally was it was a thrill,
关于这一集，有一件事让我个人印象深刻，那就是它非常令人兴奋，

215
00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:53.760
because it was hard to tell stories on other shows about characters going through internal things.
因为在其他剧里讲述角色经历内心挣扎的故事很难。

216
00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:57.560
And in this case with Michael, it was even more than that,
而在迈克尔这个案例中，情况甚至更复杂，

217
00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:01.420
because this character was going through something internal and he was unaware of it,
因为这个角色正在经历某种内心波动，但他自己却浑然不觉，

218
00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:06.280
which made it really exciting to write, because I love internal stories,
这让创作过程变得非常刺激，因为我喜欢写内心戏，

219
00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:08.900
but it also made it kind of difficult to explain at times.
但也让它有时变得难以解释。

220
00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:13.540
And I remember that I created a little chart where it said,
我记得我当时做了一张小图表，上面写着，

221
00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:16.240
here's what Michael is doing and saying in the scene.
迈克尔在这一幕里做了什么、说了什么。

222
00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:21.740
And then in bold under it, I wrote what was actually happening to Michael underneath it all.
然后在下面用粗体写着，这一切背后迈克尔到底在经历什么。

223
00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:25.100
And, of course, Steve got it all intuitively, and he's a genius.
当然，史蒂夫凭直觉就完全领会了，他真是个天才。

224
00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:29.060
It was such a treat to be able to write and tell that kind of story.
能写出并讲述那样的故事真是一种享受。

225
00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:35.860
And then, Jenna, to have you be aware of what it was that was going on with Michael,
还有，珍娜，你能意识到迈克尔身上发生了什么，

226
00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:41.360
to have Pam sort of sense it and see it and fix it without it being spoken
让帕姆在不言明的情况下感知到、看到并解决它，

227
00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:43.880
was just such a delight as a writer.
作为编剧，这真是太令人高兴了。

228
00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:45.600
Isn't that amazing?
这难道不神奇吗？

229
00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:46.900
I love it.
我喜欢。

230
00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:52.740
I love that she had, like, secret notes and charts in her script about the emotional journey
我喜欢她在剧本里为角色的情感历程做的那些秘密笔记和图表。

231
00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:53.460
of characters.
角色的情感历程。

232
00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:59.140
Yeah, I find all of that so interesting, just like the writer's process and what she wrote
是啊，我觉得这一切都太有趣了，就像编剧的创作过程，她写了什么，

233
00:10:59.140 --> 00:11:01.640
and how then it ended up playing, you know?
以及最后呈现出来的效果，你懂吗？

234
00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:02.220
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

235
00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:03.320
Angela, I just realized something.
安吉拉，我刚刚意识到一件事。

236
00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:03.760
What?
什么？

237
00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:04.820
She was tracking.
她在追踪。

238
00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:06.200
She was tracking.
她在追踪。

239
00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:08.440
Tracking Michael's emotional journey.
追踪迈克尔的情感历程。

240
00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:09.220
She tracked it.
她追踪了。

241
00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:09.740
All right.
好吧。

242
00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:12.620
Well, we are going to hear more from Jen throughout the episode.
那么，在这一集里我们还会听到更多关于珍的内容。

243
00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:14.720
So, Jenna, why don't you fast fact me?
所以，珍娜，快给我来个快速事实吧？

244
00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:18.320
Okay, I'm calling fast fact number two, The Big Fight.
好的，我宣布快速事实二号，关于《大争吵》那一集。

245
00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:20.900
Oh, you did a shoulder shimmy.
噢，你刚才抖了抖肩膀。

246
00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:21.480
I know.
我知道。

247
00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:22.180
Are you intrigued?
你感兴趣了吗？

248
00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:23.320
I am.
我很感兴趣。

249
00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:26.740
In Mindy Kaling's book, Is Everyone Hanging Out Without Me?
在敏迪·卡灵的书《大家都没带我玩吗？》里，

250
00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:32.580
She writes a chapter about working on The Office and being a writer and also being a performer.
她写了一章关于在《办公室》工作，既做编剧又做演员的经历。

251
00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:40.340
And she said in her book that she and Greg Daniels got into such a huge fight during this
她在书里提到，她和格雷格·丹尼尔斯在这一集拍摄期间大吵了一架，

252
00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:43.220
episode that she stormed off the set.
吵到她愤然离场。

253
00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:44.760
She kicked his car.
她还踢了他的车。

254
00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:45.820
Yes.
没错。

255
00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:46.840
Yes.
是的。

256
00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:48.980
Oh, that's so good.
噢，这太精彩了。

257
00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:50.220
I forgot about that.
我都忘了这事了。

258
00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:55.120
But rather than have me read you the passage, Angela, wouldn't you rather hear it in Mindy's
安吉拉，与其让我读这段文字给你听，你难道不想听听明迪本人的声音吗？

259
00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:55.420
voice?
想。

260
00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:56.760
Yes.
好的。

261
00:11:57.340 --> 00:11:58.100
Well, guess what?
那么，你猜怎么着？

262
00:11:58.420 --> 00:11:58.580
What?
怎么了？

263
00:11:58.580 --> 00:11:59.720
There's an audio book.
有有声书版本。

264
00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:02.200
Oh, oh, my God.
噢，天哪。

265
00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:02.820
Oh, my God.
天哪。

266
00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:03.660
Hit play, Sam.
播放吧，萨姆。

