小知识。

1207
00:54:32.360 --> 00:54:32.760
Tidbit.
小知识。

1208
00:54:32.900 --> 00:54:33.720
It's a Kinsey tidbit.
这是金赛的小知识。

1209
00:54:33.960 --> 00:54:41.180
All right, so when Pam does finally get back, they begin again, and Dwight is the first one to share.
好的，那么当帕姆最终回来时，他们重新开始，而德怀特是第一个分享的。

1210
00:54:41.560 --> 00:54:44.220
Oh, this is one of my favorite things.
哦，这是我最喜欢的事情之一。

1211
00:54:44.460 --> 00:54:51.520
And Dwight shares that he was supposed to have a twin, but he absorbed the twin in utero.
德怀特分享说他本该有个双胞胎兄弟，但他还在子宫里时就把对方吸收了。

1212
00:54:52.200 --> 00:54:54.920
All right, we had a fan question from Aira to Jolly.
好了，我们有一个来自艾拉给乔利的粉丝提问。

1213
00:54:55.240 --> 00:55:00.840
Did Rainn Wilson make the whole absorbing twin thing up, or was it scripted?
雷恩·威尔逊吸收双胞胎的事是他编的，还是剧本里写的？

1214
00:55:01.720 --> 00:55:05.680
Well, first of all, I will tell you, it is not in the script.
嗯，首先我要告诉你，剧本里没有这一段。

1215
00:55:06.560 --> 00:55:11.440
I don't know if Rainn made it up, but in the script, Dwight was supposed to say this.
我不知道是不是雷恩编的，但在剧本里，德怀特原本应该说的是这个。

1216
00:55:11.600 --> 00:55:12.660
He was supposed to say,
他原本应该说，

1217
00:55:13.280 --> 00:55:18.300
In the blizzard of 97, 12 shroots died in the basement of our house.
在97年的暴风雪中，12只施鲁特家的猪死在了我们家的地下室里。

1218
00:55:18.300 --> 00:55:21.480
They drank beer cider that had already turned.
它们喝了已经变质的啤酒苹果酒。

1219
00:55:22.220 --> 00:55:24.980
President McKinley declared it a national emergency.
麦金莱总统宣布这为国家紧急状态。

1220
00:55:26.180 --> 00:55:29.700
Now, my favorite thing about that is that clearly it's not 1997.
现在，关于那段话我最喜欢的一点是，显然那不是1997年。

1221
00:55:31.720 --> 00:55:33.420
It's like 1897.
那就像是1897年。

1222
00:55:33.640 --> 00:55:34.200
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

1223
00:55:34.640 --> 00:55:35.500
I guess.
我想是吧。

1224
00:55:36.240 --> 00:55:40.020
But that was originally Dwight's grief share.
但那原本是德怀特的悲伤分享。

1225
00:55:40.260 --> 00:55:41.680
So here's the thing.
所以事情是这样的。

1226
00:55:41.880 --> 00:55:47.200
I reached out to Jen Salata about this, and this is maybe one of my favorite text threads of all time.
我为此联系了简·萨拉塔，这可能是我有史以来最喜欢的短信对话之一。

1227
00:55:47.200 --> 00:55:52.340
This is what tickled me so much, is that Jen Salata, Jenna, she's one of our people.
让我觉得特别有趣的是，简·萨拉塔，珍娜，她是我们的自己人。

1228
00:55:52.620 --> 00:55:53.540
She's a deep diver.
她是个深挖细节的人。

1229
00:55:54.280 --> 00:55:54.500
Yeah.
没错。

1230
00:55:54.860 --> 00:55:59.500
The minute I asked her, she went on a deep dive for the whole afternoon.
我一问她，她就花了一整个下午去深挖这件事。

1231
00:55:59.660 --> 00:55:59.800
Ready?
准备好了吗？

1232
00:56:00.280 --> 00:56:05.220
So I say, okay, Jen, Dwight's speech about absorbing his twin is not in the script.
我说，好的，简，德怀特关于吸收双胞胎的演讲不在剧本里。

1233
00:56:05.340 --> 00:56:06.420
Was that an improv?
那是即兴发挥吗？

1234
00:56:06.420 --> 00:56:07.580
Did you tell him on the day?
你是当天告诉他的吗？

1235
00:56:07.780 --> 00:56:09.500
She goes, oh, my God.
她说，天哪。

1236
00:56:09.720 --> 00:56:10.780
I don't remember.
我不记得了。

1237
00:56:10.980 --> 00:56:11.480
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1238
00:56:11.480 --> 00:56:12.280
I love that speech.
我喜欢那段演讲。

1239
00:56:12.440 --> 00:56:13.840
And sadly, it wasn't mine.
遗憾的是，那不是我想出来的。

1240
00:56:14.280 --> 00:56:15.880
I'm going to start texting people.
我要开始发短信问人了。

1241
00:56:16.100 --> 00:56:16.680
Please hold.
请稍等。

1242
00:56:17.620 --> 00:56:21.700
And throughout the day, she said, I texted Rain.
在那一整天里，她说，我给雷恩发了短信。

1243
00:56:21.940 --> 00:56:25.300
Rain actually thinks it was an alt pitched from Paul.
雷恩其实认为那是保罗提出的备选方案。

1244
00:56:26.440 --> 00:56:28.000
Jen said, here's a side note.
简说，顺便提一下。

1245
00:56:28.180 --> 00:56:33.740
I had a friend that reabsorbed his twin, but I definitely didn't come up with the strength of a baby.
我有个朋友确实重新吸收了他的双胞胎，但我绝对没想出婴儿的力量那一出。

1246
00:56:35.240 --> 00:56:37.980
She said, I'm going to check with Paul where that part came from.
她说，我要去问问保罗那部分是从哪来的。

1247
00:56:38.240 --> 00:56:38.900
Please hold.
请稍等。

1248
00:56:39.160 --> 00:56:39.920
She texts Paul.
她给保罗发了短信。

1249
00:56:40.360 --> 00:56:42.820
Paul says he thinks it was Justin Spitzer.
保罗说他觉得那是贾斯汀·斯皮策想出来的。

1250
00:56:43.120 --> 00:56:44.020
Hold one second.
稍等一下。

1251
00:56:44.320 --> 00:56:45.440
Now texting Justin.
现在给贾斯汀发短信。

1252
00:56:45.720 --> 00:56:47.160
Justin was another one of our writers.
贾斯汀是我们另一位编剧。

1253
00:56:47.160 --> 00:56:49.920
This is what Justin texted Jen back.
这是贾斯汀回给珍的短信内容。

1254
00:56:50.140 --> 00:56:55.580
I still remember that because it was early season three and I was so nervous about proving myself.
我至今还记得，因为那是第三季早期，我当时非常紧张，急于证明自己。

1255
00:56:55.880 --> 00:56:58.140
I guess, yes, I came up with it.
我想，是的，是我提出的这个点子。

1256
00:56:58.220 --> 00:57:05.440
But the thing that really sold it to me was the last line about him having the strength of a grown man plus a baby.
但真正打动我的是最后那句关于他拥有成年男人外加一个婴儿的力量的台词。

1257
00:57:05.440 --> 00:57:09.100
And that was something that Paul Lieberstein added after.
那是保罗·利伯斯坦后来加进去的。

1258
00:57:09.360 --> 00:57:12.400
So I think he deserves a fair amount of credit as well.
所以我认为他也理应获得相当多的功劳。

1259
00:57:12.400 --> 00:57:17.420
So I'm giving that a slow clap.
所以我现在要为他缓慢鼓掌。

1260
00:57:17.440 --> 00:57:18.060
A slow clap.
缓慢鼓掌。

1261
00:57:18.260 --> 00:57:20.020
Into a big clap.
变成热烈鼓掌。

1262
00:57:20.500 --> 00:57:20.820
Yes.
是的。

1263
00:57:21.680 --> 00:57:22.240
Wow.
哇。

1264
00:57:22.540 --> 00:57:25.040
It was a two-hander that Paul and Justin pitched.
这是一个保罗和贾斯汀共同提出的双人戏份。

1265
00:57:25.560 --> 00:57:31.300
I love that we got to the bottom of that mystery because it is one of my all-time favorite Dwight-isMs.
我很高兴我们弄清了这个谜团，因为这是我个人最喜欢的德怀特语录之一。

1266
00:57:32.100 --> 00:57:36.660
Also, guys, Justin Spitzer is the creator of the show Superstore.
另外，伙计们，贾斯汀·斯皮策是剧集《爆笑超市》的创作者。

1267
00:57:37.000 --> 00:57:39.080
Justin is so talented.
贾斯汀太有才了。

1268
00:57:39.340 --> 00:57:40.240
He's so talented.
他真的非常有才华。

1269
00:57:40.240 --> 00:57:40.840
I love him.
我爱他。

1270
00:57:40.960 --> 00:57:41.380
Love him.
爱他。

1271
00:57:41.900 --> 00:57:42.420
Anyway.
总之。

1272
00:57:42.760 --> 00:57:47.360
I think the only place to go from here is back to our grief circle.
我觉得接下来我们只能回到悲伤辅导圈了。

1273
00:57:47.760 --> 00:57:49.960
And we need to hear from some others.
我们需要听听其他人的想法。

1274
00:57:50.420 --> 00:57:50.680
Okay.
好的。

1275
00:57:50.760 --> 00:57:53.200
So we're back into the grief counseling scene.
我们回到了悲伤辅导的场景。

1276
00:57:53.240 --> 00:57:54.680
And Stanley has just refused.
斯坦利拒绝参与。

1277
00:57:54.680 --> 00:57:56.280
He is not going to participate.
他不想参加。

1278
00:57:56.540 --> 00:57:56.680
No.
不。

1279
00:57:57.120 --> 00:57:58.900
He chunks that ball back at Michael.
他把球扔回给了迈克尔。

1280
00:57:59.420 --> 00:57:59.800
Hey.
嘿。

1281
00:57:59.900 --> 00:58:00.500
I heard that.
我听到了。

1282
00:58:00.640 --> 00:58:01.260
Yeah, you heard that.
没错，你听到了。

1283
00:58:01.260 --> 00:58:03.840
But Pam agrees to participate.
但帕姆同意参与。

1284
00:58:04.160 --> 00:58:06.840
And she's going to share a story about her family.
她打算分享一个关于她家庭的故事。

1285
00:58:07.020 --> 00:58:11.380
But it's clearly just the synopsis for the movie Million Dollar Baby.
但那显然只是电影《百万美元宝贝》的剧情梗概。

1286
00:58:12.160 --> 00:58:12.340
Yeah.
没错。

1287
00:58:12.720 --> 00:58:14.400
I mean, again, Pam is now the gem.
我是说，帕姆现在真是个宝藏。

1288
00:58:14.660 --> 00:58:15.480
She's the jokester.
她是那个爱开玩笑的人。

1289
00:58:16.160 --> 00:58:16.700
Yes.
是的。

1290
00:58:16.900 --> 00:58:22.680
And then Ryan joins in and he shares a story that is very clearly the Lion King.
然后瑞安也加入了，他分享的故事显然就是《狮子王》。

1291
00:58:22.980 --> 00:58:24.820
I mean, he says the word Mufasa.
我是说，他甚至直接说了“木法沙”这个词。

1292
00:58:25.100 --> 00:58:26.580
I mean, come on.
拜托，别闹了。

1293
00:58:26.580 --> 00:58:30.360
But then Kevin catches on and he's tickled.
但接着凯文也反应过来了，他觉得很有趣。

1294
00:58:30.560 --> 00:58:31.540
He wants to participate.
他也想参与。

1295
00:58:31.540 --> 00:58:32.840
He wants to play the game.
他想玩这个游戏。

1296
00:58:32.960 --> 00:58:35.400
But he goes too broad, too on the nose.
但他表现得太明显、太直白了。

1297
00:58:35.560 --> 00:58:37.980
And he basically breaks down Weekend at Bernie's.
他基本上把《老板度假》的剧情给复述了一遍。

1298
00:58:38.080 --> 00:58:39.740
And Michael's like, what?
迈克尔当时反应是，什么？

1299
00:58:39.920 --> 00:58:40.600
Hold up.
等等。

1300
00:58:41.000 --> 00:58:41.860
That's a movie.
那是一部电影。

1301
00:58:42.160 --> 00:58:43.440
And he gets really ticked off.
而且他真的被惹火了。

1302
00:58:43.620 --> 00:58:43.760
Okay.
好的。

1303
00:58:43.820 --> 00:58:48.580
So there was a lot of curiosity about these movie plots in the conference room.
所以会议室里大家对这些电影情节都很好奇。

1304
00:58:48.740 --> 00:58:52.080
We got a fan question from Tristan who wants to know,
我们收到了一位粉丝Tristan的提问，他想知道，

1305
00:58:52.220 --> 00:58:55.060
when everyone is in the conference room for Michael's counseling session,
当大家都在会议室参加迈克尔的心理辅导课时，

1306
00:58:55.060 --> 00:58:59.580
did the cast improvise the movie plots that were mentioned or were they scripted?
提到的那些电影情节是演员即兴发挥的，还是剧本里写好的？

1307
00:58:59.740 --> 00:59:01.700
Jenna, to my knowledge, they were all scripted.
珍娜，据我所知，它们都是剧本里写好的。

1308
00:59:01.840 --> 00:59:02.860
That's how I remember it.
我的记忆也是这样。

1309
00:59:03.540 --> 00:59:03.840
Yes.
是的。

1310
00:59:03.980 --> 00:59:05.480
I looked these up in the shooting draft.
我查了拍摄剧本。

1311
00:59:05.740 --> 00:59:12.020
And Pam's Million Dollar Baby story and Kevin's Weekend at Bernie story are both in the script.
帕姆的《百万美元宝贝》故事和凯文的《老板度假》故事都在剧本里。

1312
00:59:12.200 --> 00:59:15.840
However, Ryan's fake movie story is different.
不过，瑞安那个虚构的电影故事不一样。

1313
00:59:16.280 --> 00:59:16.660
Ah.
啊。

1314
00:59:17.380 --> 00:59:17.840
Yes.
是的。

1315
00:59:17.840 --> 00:59:21.140
In the script, he talks about Thelma and Louise.
在剧本里，他讲的是《末路狂花》。

1316
00:59:22.100 --> 00:59:22.340
Well.
好吧。

1317
00:59:22.340 --> 00:59:23.560
This is what he says.
他是这么说的。

1318
00:59:23.560 --> 00:59:24.860
He says,
他说，

1319
00:59:25.300 --> 00:59:28.240
My mom's sister Thelma died last year.
我妈的姐妹塞尔玛去年去世了。

1320
00:59:28.880 --> 00:59:31.520
She was with her friend named Lucy.
她当时和她的朋友露西在一起。

1321
00:59:32.780 --> 00:59:34.920
A cop was trying to pull them over.
有个警察想让她们靠边停车。

1322
00:59:35.080 --> 00:59:39.400
And I guess the brakes must have not been working because they ended up driving over a cliff.
我猜刹车肯定失灵了，因为她们最后开车冲下了悬崖。

1323
00:59:39.580 --> 00:59:41.680
And it was a total shock to everyone.
这对所有人来说都是个巨大的打击。

1324
00:59:42.140 --> 00:59:42.500
Okay.
好的。

1325
00:59:42.760 --> 00:59:45.220
Well, we wanted to get to the bottom of this.
嗯，我们想弄清真相。

1326
00:59:45.380 --> 00:59:49.980
So we reached out to the source, the writer of this episode, Jen Salata.
所以我们联系了消息来源，也就是这一集的编剧简·萨拉塔。

1327
00:59:50.260 --> 00:59:52.160
And this is what she had to say.
她是这么说的。

1328
00:59:52.160 --> 00:59:56.920
For the movies and the grief counseling session, I was really excited.
关于电影和悲伤辅导课，我当时真的很兴奋。

1329
00:59:56.920 --> 00:59:58.600
It was really fun to think about.
构思这些情节真的很有趣。

1330
00:59:58.900 --> 01:00:09.220
I went off on script and needed to find a way that everybody would sit there with Michael Scott and not share their own personal stories of huge loss.
我当时在写剧本，需要想个办法让大家坐在迈克尔·斯科特身边，却又不会分享他们自己关于重大损失的个人故事。

1331
01:00:09.220 --> 01:00:12.040
Because it just didn't seem like they would do that.
因为他们看起来根本不会那样做。

1332
01:00:12.220 --> 01:00:18.260
So I thought they should share movies plot lines as if they were their own lives.
所以我想到他们应该分享电影情节，就好像那是他们自己的生活一样。

1333
01:00:18.260 --> 01:00:23.640
And I came up with Million Dollar Baby for you, Jenna, for Pam.
我为你，也就是帕姆，想到了《百万美元宝贝》。

1334
01:00:23.800 --> 01:00:28.400
And then also for Kevin, Weekend at Bernie's.
还有凯文的《老板度假》。

1335
01:00:28.400 --> 01:00:31.420
And for Ryan, I had a different one.
至于瑞安，我原本想的是另一个。

1336
01:00:31.820 --> 01:00:34.280
I think BJ came up with The Lion King.
我觉得是BJ想到了《狮子王》。

1337
01:00:34.540 --> 01:00:36.460
I don't quite remember, but I think it was BJ.
我记不太清了，但我觉得应该是BJ。

1338
01:00:36.760 --> 01:00:37.940
And I love that one.
我很喜欢那个版本。

1339
01:00:38.520 --> 01:00:42.120
The one I had, I actually found my first draft of the script.
我原本想的那个，我其实找到了剧本的初稿。

1340
01:00:42.560 --> 01:00:43.760
I had Ryan.
我给瑞安写的是这个。

1341
01:00:43.760 --> 01:00:45.000
I'll read you the line.
我读给你听。

1342
01:00:45.200 --> 01:00:46.780
It's not as good as The Lion King one.
没《狮子王》那个好。

1343
01:00:46.780 --> 01:00:49.980
But I have Ryan say, this is almost too horrible to talk about.
但我让瑞安说，这事太可怕了，简直难以启齿。

1344
01:00:49.980 --> 01:00:52.080
But I had a cousin who was a big city lawyer.
但我有个表亲是个大城市的律师。

1345
01:00:52.080 --> 01:00:54.660
And he was visiting an Amish town not far from here.
他去离这儿不远的一个阿米什小镇参观。

1346
01:00:54.780 --> 01:00:56.940
And he was smothered to death in their grain silo.
结果他在他们的谷仓里被闷死了。

1347
01:00:57.220 --> 01:01:00.000
And then I had Michael say, ooh, that must have made you really sad.
然后我让迈克尔说，噢，那一定让你很难过吧。

1348
01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:00.420
Did it?
是吗？

1349
01:01:00.480 --> 01:01:01.340
And Ryan says, yes.
瑞安说，是的。

1350
01:01:01.700 --> 01:01:04.420
So I think that was a witness.
所以我认为那是一个证人。

1351
01:01:04.620 --> 01:01:05.740
So I had Ryan's from Witness.
所以我用了瑞安在《证人》里的桥段。

1352
01:01:05.940 --> 01:01:10.620
I wish I could remember some of the other ones because I feel like we had other ones that we pitched on.
真希望我还能想起其他的，因为我觉得我们当时还构思过别的。

1353
01:01:10.740 --> 01:01:13.240
But those were the ones from my first draft.
但那些是我初稿里的内容。

1354
01:01:13.240 --> 01:01:16.080
And then, of course, the Lion King circle of life was fantastic.
当然，《狮子王》里的“生生不息”那段简直太棒了。

1355
01:01:16.080 --> 01:01:20.820
And Ryan saying, it'll take about an hour and a half to tell it was like such a great line.
瑞安说“讲完它得花一个半小时”，这句台词真是绝了。

1356
01:01:21.800 --> 01:01:23.000
That is amazing.
太精彩了。

1357
01:01:23.180 --> 01:01:25.540
By the way, my college roommate and I used to watch Witness.
顺便说一下，我和大学室友以前常看《证人》。

1358
01:01:25.900 --> 01:01:29.500
And we would say to each other all the time, be careful out among them English.
我们总是对彼此说：“在那些英国人中间要小心点。”

1359
01:01:30.920 --> 01:01:31.640
Thank you.
谢谢。

1360
01:01:31.960 --> 01:01:34.620
That is my movie quote from Witness.
那就是我从《证人》里学到的电影台词。

1361
01:01:35.020 --> 01:01:39.220
But isn't that wild, Jenna, that Ryan's movie went through three versions.
但珍娜，瑞安的电影经历了三个版本，这不是很疯狂吗？

1362
01:01:39.220 --> 01:01:40.000
It was Witness.
先是《证人》。

1363
01:01:40.000 --> 01:01:43.080
And then it was, I guess, Thelma and Louise, according to your script.
然后根据你的剧本，我猜是《末路狂花》。

1364
01:01:43.240 --> 01:01:45.840
But The Lion King is what made it in the show.
但最终出现在剧里的是《狮子王》。

1365
01:01:46.740 --> 01:01:51.480
Yeah, clearly they had a lot of alts for these movie plots.
是啊，显然他们为这些电影情节准备了很多备选方案。

1366
01:01:51.520 --> 01:01:54.220
But all of them were scripted, guys.
但伙计们，这些全都是写在剧本里的。

1367
01:01:54.460 --> 01:01:56.380
All of them written by our awesome writers.
全都是我们出色的编剧写出来的。

1368
01:01:56.560 --> 01:01:58.140
We did not improvise that stuff.
我们并没有即兴发挥那些内容。

1369
01:01:58.560 --> 01:01:59.400
Love that.
太喜欢这个了。

1370
01:01:59.500 --> 01:02:01.460
Love that little tidbit, Jen Salata.
喜欢这个小花絮，珍·萨拉塔。

1371
01:02:01.660 --> 01:02:07.560
So, guys, Michael gets pretty upset that people are not taking this seriously.
那么，伙计们，迈克尔因为大家没把这件事当回事而感到非常沮丧。

1372
01:02:08.100 --> 01:02:14.600
You know, he says the guy who used to do his job and sit at his desk has died and no one cares.
你知道，他说那个曾经做他这份工作、坐在他办公桌前的人去世了，却没人关心。

1373
01:02:14.940 --> 01:02:15.100
Yeah.
没错。

1374
01:02:16.200 --> 01:02:21.260
And Toby tries to talk him down and tries to explain that this is just life.
托比试图安抚他，解释说这就是生活。

1375
01:02:21.260 --> 01:02:26.400
And that this morning he saw a bird fly into the window downstairs and die.
还说他今天早上看到一只鸟撞到楼下的窗户死掉了。

1376
01:02:27.400 --> 01:02:28.540
Michael freaks out.
迈克尔崩溃了。

1377
01:02:28.920 --> 01:02:29.700
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1378
01:02:29.820 --> 01:02:30.080
Toby.
托比。

1379
01:02:30.360 --> 01:02:31.680
Toby, what are you thinking?
托比，你在想什么呢？

1380
01:02:32.040 --> 01:02:34.120
He totally attaches to that.
他完全被这件事吸引住了。

1381
01:02:34.420 --> 01:02:38.220
Now Michael's grief for Ed is somehow wrapped into this bird.
现在迈克尔对埃德的哀悼不知怎么就转移到了这只鸟身上。

1382
01:02:38.220 --> 01:02:40.040
It's going to be a whole thing.
这下可要闹出大动静了。

1383
01:02:40.380 --> 01:02:40.600
Yeah.
是啊。

1384
01:02:40.780 --> 01:02:42.100
He runs downstairs.
他跑下楼去。

1385
01:02:42.160 --> 01:02:43.440
He freaks out.
他抓狂了。

1386
01:02:43.600 --> 01:02:45.280
He wants to see if the bird is alive.
他想看看那只鸟是不是还活着。

1387
01:02:46.080 --> 01:02:48.560
I had a fan catch here from Kendra.
我这里有一个来自肯德拉的粉丝发现。

1388
01:02:49.460 --> 01:02:56.040
At 14 minutes, 33 seconds, when Michael runs through the front door to get the bird, he runs past the security desk.
在14分33秒时，当迈克尔跑过前门去救那只鸟时，他跑过了保安台。

1389
01:02:56.200 --> 01:02:58.440
And the security guard is not Hank.
那个保安不是汉克。

1390
01:02:58.720 --> 01:03:00.680
Oh, good catch.
哦，好眼力。

1391
01:03:01.220 --> 01:03:03.180
Yeah, different security guard.
没错，是另一个保安。

1392
01:03:03.340 --> 01:03:05.200
Hank took a personal day, you guys.
伙计们，汉克请了事假。

1393
01:03:05.200 --> 01:03:06.260
I guess so.
我想是吧。

1394
01:03:06.400 --> 01:03:09.500
Well, Michael attempts to resuscitate the bird in the kitchen.
好吧，迈克尔试图在厨房里给那只鸟做心肺复苏。

1395
01:03:10.140 --> 01:03:11.520
Angela, you're not pleased.
安吉拉，你看起来很不高兴。

1396
01:03:11.880 --> 01:03:14.520
So Michael is determined to save this bird.
所以迈克尔决心要救活这只鸟。

1397
01:03:14.720 --> 01:03:16.140
He brings it into the kitchen.
他把它带进了厨房。

1398
01:03:16.640 --> 01:03:18.860
Angela Martin is not pleased.
安吉拉·马丁很不高兴。

1399
01:03:19.100 --> 01:03:21.000
She's like, no, that shouldn't be in here.
她觉得，不行，那东西不该出现在这儿。

1400
01:03:21.340 --> 01:03:21.980
Get it out.
把它弄出去。

1401
01:03:22.220 --> 01:03:23.580
Well, she is not pleased.
嗯，她很不高兴。

1402
01:03:23.640 --> 01:03:24.820
And Angela, she's not wrong.
而且安吉拉，她说得没错。

1403
01:03:25.080 --> 01:03:25.980
Thank you.
谢谢。

1404
01:03:26.240 --> 01:03:27.260
Thank you, Jenna.
谢谢你，珍娜。

1405
01:03:27.820 --> 01:03:28.580
You're welcome.
不客气。

1406
01:03:28.880 --> 01:03:29.640
You're welcome.
不客气。

1407
01:03:29.880 --> 01:03:32.700
We had a fan question from Ellie Friedlander.
我们收到了一位粉丝艾莉·弗里德兰德的提问。

1408
01:03:32.700 --> 01:03:36.340
She wants to know, was that a real dead bird?
她想知道，那真的是一只死鸟吗？

1409
01:03:37.540 --> 01:03:38.180
No.
不是。

1410
01:03:38.420 --> 01:03:39.280
No, no.
不是，不是。

1411
01:03:39.280 --> 01:03:39.840
No, Ellie.
不是的，艾莉。

1412
01:03:40.080 --> 01:03:42.000
It was a fake bird.
那是只假鸟。

1413
01:03:42.200 --> 01:03:43.880
I reached out to Phil.
我联系了菲尔。

1414
01:03:44.120 --> 01:03:51.640
He told me that he found three dead fake bird options and presented them to Jen, Roger, our director, and Greg.
他告诉我，他找了三个死鸟道具供选择，并把它们展示给了简、我们的导演罗杰，还有格雷格看。

1415
01:03:51.640 --> 01:03:54.280
They chose the one that you see in the show.
他们选了你在剧中看到的那一个。

1416
01:03:54.460 --> 01:04:03.120
And Angela, I have to say, when he texted me back that he presented the three dead birds, I imagined in my head that they were on a silver tray.
安吉拉，我得说，当他回短信说他展示了那三只死鸟时，我脑子里想象的是它们被放在银托盘上。

1417
01:04:03.500 --> 01:04:07.340
Because remember, Phil would always present you your props on a silver tray.
因为你要记得，菲尔总是会用银托盘把道具呈给你。

1418
01:04:07.740 --> 01:04:08.380
Yes, yes.
没错，没错。

1419
01:04:08.380 --> 01:04:10.840
And I was just imagining it.
我当时就在脑补那个画面。

1420
01:04:10.840 --> 01:04:14.040
And I wrote him back and I said, Phil, were they on a silver tray?
我回信问他：菲尔，它们是在银托盘上吗？

1421
01:04:14.040 --> 01:04:15.820
And he said, you know me too well.
他说：你太了解我了。

1422
01:04:17.600 --> 01:04:21.400
These are the moments in our show where I'm like, hey, babe, how was your day?
这就是我们剧组里那些时刻，我会问：嘿，宝贝，你今天过得怎么样？

1423
01:04:21.480 --> 01:04:22.040
What did you do today?
你今天都做了什么？

1424
01:04:22.740 --> 01:04:25.640
Well, I had to find three fake dead birds.
哦，我得去找三只假死鸟。

1425
01:04:26.620 --> 01:04:26.900
Yeah.
是啊。

1426
01:04:27.360 --> 01:04:28.120
I scoured.
我到处搜罗。

1427
01:04:28.120 --> 01:04:34.020
Or like when Greg goes home and his wife, Susanna, is like, hey, hon, how'd it go shooting today?
或者就像格雷格回家时，他妻子苏珊娜问：嘿，亲爱的，今天拍摄怎么样？

1428
01:04:34.020 --> 01:04:34.780
He's like, great.
他说：棒极了。

1429
01:04:34.780 --> 01:04:36.000
I picked a dead bird.
我挑了一只死鸟。

1430
01:04:36.280 --> 01:04:36.620
Yeah.
是啊。

1431
01:04:37.100 --> 01:04:38.360
I picked the yellow one.
我选了黄色的那只。

1432
01:04:38.500 --> 01:04:39.900
I made my dead bird selection.
我做出了我的死鸟选择。

1433
01:04:40.720 --> 01:04:41.820
Yes, exactly.
没错，正是这样。

1434
01:04:42.380 --> 01:04:46.200
Well, Michael then tells the staff, attention, attention.
嗯，迈克尔随后告诉员工们：注意，注意。

1435
01:04:46.220 --> 01:04:49.220
We are holding a funeral for this bird at 4 p.m.
我们将在下午4点为这只鸟举行葬礼。

1436
01:04:49.360 --> 01:04:50.180
in the parking lot.
就在停车场。

1437
01:04:50.400 --> 01:04:50.780
Be there.
务必参加。

1438
01:04:51.080 --> 01:04:51.840
It's on.
活动开始。

1439
01:04:52.260 --> 01:04:54.980
Jenna, now I think it's time to check back in on Jim and Karen.
珍娜，我觉得现在是时候看看吉姆和凯伦那边的情况了。

1440
01:04:56.240 --> 01:04:57.140
Oh, yes.
哦，没错。

1441
01:04:57.800 --> 01:04:59.260
Have they found the chips?
他们找到薯片了吗？

1442
01:05:00.120 --> 01:05:00.920
What's the status?
进展如何？

1443
01:05:01.280 --> 01:05:06.200
Where are they in their search for this very hard to find potato chip bag?
他们在寻找这包极难买到的薯片时进展到哪一步了？

1444
01:05:06.820 --> 01:05:08.520
That's actually in the vending machine.
其实就在自动贩卖机里。

1445
01:05:08.560 --> 01:05:09.960
That might be in the vending machine.
那可能就在自动贩卖机里。

1446
01:05:10.360 --> 01:05:11.980
That is in the vending machine.
那就在自动贩卖机里。

1447
01:05:13.320 --> 01:05:17.140
That, according to a fan catch, is B1 in the vending machine.
根据一位粉丝的发现，那就在自动贩卖机的B1位置。

1448
01:05:17.500 --> 01:05:19.160
Yeah, it's right there waiting for them.
没错，它就在那儿等着他们呢。

1449
01:05:20.100 --> 01:05:26.680
Well, Karen kind of impresses Jim because she decides to call Montreal, the Montreal factory,
嗯，凯伦让吉姆刮目相看，因为她决定给蒙特利尔，也就是蒙特利尔工厂打电话，

1450
01:05:26.680 --> 01:05:27.780
to see if they have them.
看看他们那边有没有货。

1451
01:05:27.900 --> 01:05:29.440
And she speaks French.
而且她会说法语。

1452
01:05:30.160 --> 01:05:30.580
May we.
我们可以吗？

1453
01:05:30.780 --> 01:05:31.540
May we.
我们可以吗？

1454
01:05:31.660 --> 01:05:32.180
May we.
我们可以吗？

1455
01:05:32.320 --> 01:05:34.300
A lot of people wrote in about this.
很多人写信问过这个问题。

1456
01:05:34.740 --> 01:05:39.940
Brianna Bullard and many, many others want to know, does Rashida Jones actually know French?
布里安娜·布拉德和许多许多人都想知道，拉什达·琼斯真的会法语吗？

1457
01:05:40.580 --> 01:05:42.480
So I texted Rashida.
所以我给拉什达发了条短信。

1458
01:05:42.640 --> 01:05:48.100
Since we're already texting about her breakfast order, she's probably like, Angela, what is happening?
既然我们已经在发短信讨论她的早餐订单了，她大概会想，安吉拉，这到底是怎么回事？

1459
01:05:49.400 --> 01:05:50.900
This is what she said.
她是这么说的。

1460
01:05:51.080 --> 01:05:54.640
She goes, no, at this time, I didn't know French.
她说，不，当时我并不会法语。

1461
01:05:54.640 --> 01:05:57.520
I worked really hard on that line.
那句台词我练得非常辛苦。

1462
01:05:57.580 --> 01:06:04.640
But a few years later, I ended up going to France to do a French immersion school in the south of France.
但几年后，我最终去了法国，在法国南部参加了一个法语沉浸式学校。

1463
01:06:05.140 --> 01:06:09.000
Maybe this scene was the beginning and it got me inspired.
也许那场戏是个开端，激发了我的灵感。

1464
01:06:10.140 --> 01:06:10.700
Wow.
哇。

1465
01:06:11.280 --> 01:06:12.220
That's crazy.
太不可思议了。

1466
01:06:12.220 --> 01:06:14.820
She did not speak French, but now she does.
她当时不会说法语，但现在会了。

1467
01:06:15.140 --> 01:06:15.500
Yes.
是的。

1468
01:06:15.600 --> 01:06:19.160
I was like, I want to go to a French immersion class in the south of France.
我当时就想，我想去法国南部上法语沉浸课。

1469
01:06:19.160 --> 01:06:20.400
That sounds amazing.
听起来太棒了。

1470
01:06:21.300 --> 01:06:21.700
Same.
我也是。

1471
01:06:22.820 --> 01:06:23.220
Same.
我也是。

1472
01:06:23.220 --> 01:06:24.520
I took French in high school.
我高中时学过法语。

1473
01:06:25.020 --> 01:06:25.560
You did?
你学过？

1474
01:06:25.820 --> 01:06:28.080
Oh, I have a story about that, actually.
哦，其实我有个关于那个的故事。

1475
01:06:28.360 --> 01:06:28.680
Yeah.
是吗。

1476
01:06:28.700 --> 01:06:30.120
Can I tell this real quickly?
我能快速讲一下吗？

1477
01:06:30.380 --> 01:06:30.640
Yeah.
可以。

1478
01:06:30.840 --> 01:06:32.980
I took French in high school from Sister Landry.
我高中时是跟兰德里修女学的法语。

1479
01:06:33.160 --> 01:06:34.320
I went to a Catholic school.
我上的是天主教学校。

1480
01:06:34.480 --> 01:06:36.300
Sister Landry was my French teacher.
兰德里修女是我的法语老师。

1481
01:06:37.100 --> 01:06:42.900
And I dreamed, I told you guys this before, I dreamed from the time I was a little girl that I would one day go to Paris.
我从小就梦想着有一天能去巴黎，我之前跟你们说过。

1482
01:06:43.280 --> 01:06:45.520
And then in my 30s, it finally happened.
然后在我30多岁的时候，梦想终于实现了。

1483
01:06:45.660 --> 01:06:48.840
Of course, at this point, I was now very far from my French training.
当然，那时候我已经把法语忘得差不多了。

1484
01:06:49.880 --> 01:06:51.480
I couldn't really speak French.
我其实已经不会说法语了。

1485
01:06:51.800 --> 01:06:54.460
But Lee and I, we went to a little farmer's market.
但我和李去了个小农贸市场。

1486
01:06:54.540 --> 01:06:58.040
And I guess in France, you don't touch the fruit.
我猜在法国，你是不能随便摸水果的。

1487
01:06:58.240 --> 01:06:58.820
Uh-oh.
糟糕。

1488
01:06:58.980 --> 01:06:59.200
Okay?
懂吗？

1489
01:06:59.500 --> 01:07:02.220
You don't select your own produce.
你不能自己挑选农产品。

1490
01:07:02.720 --> 01:07:08.440
You point to it or you trust the person selling the produce to select the best pieces for you.
你要么指给对方看，要么就信任卖菜的人，让他们为你挑选最好的。

1491
01:07:09.480 --> 01:07:10.900
I didn't know this.
我当时不知道这一点。

1492
01:07:11.020 --> 01:07:11.280
Okay?
懂吗？

1493
01:07:11.640 --> 01:07:12.640
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1494
01:07:12.780 --> 01:07:16.480
I would have been, I pick up things, I thump them, I smell them.
要是我的话，我肯定会去拿，去敲敲它们，闻闻它们。

1495
01:07:16.480 --> 01:07:17.620
No, lady.
不行，女士。

1496
01:07:17.800 --> 01:07:18.080
Uh-oh.
糟糕。

1497
01:07:18.080 --> 01:07:18.600
Don't do it.
别那样做。

1498
01:07:18.640 --> 01:07:18.920
Uh-oh.
糟糕。

1499
01:07:18.920 --> 01:07:22.340
If you go to a farmer's market in France, here's my hot tip for you.
如果你去法国的农贸市场，这是我给你的小贴士。

1500
01:07:22.400 --> 01:07:23.680
Do not touch that fruit.
千万别碰那些水果。

1501
01:07:23.960 --> 01:07:24.900
Don't thump the melon.
别拍那个瓜。

1502
01:07:24.900 --> 01:07:26.320
Don't thump the melon in France.
在法国别拍那个瓜。

1503
01:07:26.500 --> 01:07:26.760
Okay?
好吗？

1504
01:07:26.920 --> 01:07:27.160
Okay.
好的。

1505
01:07:27.440 --> 01:07:32.920
Now, all through this trip, we'd been going to restaurants and we'd been going to tourist places.
这次旅行全程，我们一直在去各种餐厅和旅游景点。

1506
01:07:32.920 --> 01:07:35.240
And I was just fumbling with my French.
而我的法语一直说得磕磕绊绊。

1507
01:07:35.360 --> 01:07:36.520
I couldn't get anything out.
我什么都说不出来。

1508
01:07:36.520 --> 01:07:39.840
I could read the menus, but I couldn't order anything.
我能看懂菜单，但就是点不了菜。

1509
01:07:40.220 --> 01:07:43.680
I was, I thought I was going to really help us, but I couldn't help us.
我本以为自己能帮上忙，结果却帮不上。

1510
01:07:43.780 --> 01:07:44.640
But here we are.
但现在我们到了这里。

1511
01:07:44.760 --> 01:07:46.000
We're at this little market.
我们在一个小集市上。

1512
01:07:46.220 --> 01:07:47.920
I have done the faux pas.
我犯了个错误。

1513
01:07:48.200 --> 01:07:49.200
I believe that's French.
我想这是法语词。

1514
01:07:49.380 --> 01:07:51.520
The faux pas of touching the fruit.
触碰水果的错误。

1515
01:07:52.020 --> 01:07:57.980
And this woman turns to her co-worker and goes off on me.
然后那个女人转向她的同事，开始对我大发雷霆。

1516
01:07:57.980 --> 01:08:04.060
She, in French, is calling me, like, kind of like a dumb American.
她用法语骂我，大概就是说我是个愚蠢的美国人。

1517
01:08:04.520 --> 01:08:04.920
You're a piece of trash.
你就是个垃圾。

1518
01:08:04.920 --> 01:08:10.240
