Mandy说，好吧，抱歉。

1669
01:14:31.940 --> 01:14:35.940
I can't believe there are actually people out there who are okay with Jim hooking up with Karen.
我真不敢相信竟然有人能接受吉姆和凯伦在一起。

1670
01:14:36.140 --> 01:14:37.020
That's what I remember.
这正是我记忆中的样子。

1671
01:14:38.080 --> 01:14:39.280
But Kim E.
但Kim E.

1672
01:14:39.520 --> 01:14:40.300
said this.
说了这个。

1673
01:14:41.220 --> 01:14:41.540
Hmm.
嗯。

1674
01:14:41.940 --> 01:14:44.240
Jim likes to buy chips for all his ladies.
吉姆喜欢给他的所有女士买薯片。

1675
01:14:45.700 --> 01:14:47.320
And I'm with you, Kim.
Kim，我和你站在一起。

1676
01:14:48.400 --> 01:14:51.340
As Pam, I'm like, oh, is this what you do?
作为帕姆，我的反应是，噢，这就是你的套路吗？

1677
01:14:51.720 --> 01:14:54.700
You just find all the girls their favorite chips?
你就是给所有女孩找她们最喜欢的薯片？

1678
01:14:55.080 --> 01:14:55.220
Yeah.
没错。

1679
01:14:55.480 --> 01:14:56.280
That's his game.
这就是他的套路。

1680
01:14:57.160 --> 01:14:58.400
Are we saying that right?
我们说对了吗？

1681
01:14:58.660 --> 01:14:59.020
Oh.
噢。

1682
01:14:59.340 --> 01:15:00.000
Is that your game?
那是你的套路吗？

1683
01:15:00.160 --> 01:15:00.420
You and I?
你和我？

1684
01:15:00.680 --> 01:15:02.100
I 100% doubt we are.
我百分之百怀疑我们不是。

1685
01:15:02.100 --> 01:15:02.480
I'm sure we are.
我肯定我们是。

1686
01:15:02.520 --> 01:15:03.980
Oh, Sam's giving us an okay.
噢，萨姆给我们比了个OK。

1687
01:15:03.980 --> 01:15:04.920
Sam gave us an okay.
萨姆给了我们一个OK的手势。

1688
01:15:05.120 --> 01:15:06.020
That's his game.
这就是他的套路。

1689
01:15:06.780 --> 01:15:07.460
All right.
好吧。

1690
01:15:07.600 --> 01:15:09.280
Should we go to this bird funeral, Angela?
我们要去参加这场鸟的葬礼吗，安吉拉？

1691
01:15:09.560 --> 01:15:10.440
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

1692
01:15:11.000 --> 01:15:12.340
Please take me there.
请带我去吧。

1693
01:15:12.340 --> 01:15:17.280
Well, we're out in the driveway, really, next to the warehouse.
嗯，我们实际上是在仓库旁边的车道上。

1694
01:15:17.660 --> 01:15:23.100
This was an actual parking lot that we used, and it was right next to the warehouse, and
这是一个我们实际使用的停车场，就在仓库旁边，然后

1695
01:15:23.100 --> 01:15:24.240
that's where we filmed this.
我们就是在那儿拍的这一幕。

1696
01:15:25.000 --> 01:15:28.220
Michael is very moved by Pam's beautiful coffin.
迈克尔被帕姆做的精美棺材深深打动了。

1697
01:15:28.760 --> 01:15:34.940
It starts with Pam saying a few words about the bird, but we slowly realize that Pam is speaking
开头是帕姆为这只鸟说了几句话，但我们慢慢意识到，帕姆虽然是在说

1698
01:15:34.940 --> 01:15:37.560
about the bird, but she's speaking to Michael.
这只鸟，但她其实是在对迈克尔说。

1699
01:15:37.880 --> 01:15:40.660
About his feelings about death and loss.
关于他对死亡和失去的感受。

1700
01:15:40.660 --> 01:15:43.020
And about his aloneness.
以及关于他的孤独。

1701
01:15:43.720 --> 01:15:50.480
She talks a lot about how just because the bird was alone doesn't mean he was unloved,
她说了好多，说那只鸟虽然孤单，并不代表它没人爱，

1702
01:15:50.680 --> 01:15:54.700
that he was very loved and respected by the other birds.
说它深受其他鸟儿的爱戴和尊重。

1703
01:15:54.960 --> 01:15:56.420
And then she sings a song.
然后她唱了一首歌。

1704
01:15:56.640 --> 01:15:58.880
I was very surprised by this for Pam.
这让我对帕姆刮目相看。

1705
01:15:59.140 --> 01:16:00.660
She really put herself out there.
她真的豁出去了。

1706
01:16:00.780 --> 01:16:02.780
She sings On the Wings of Love.
她唱的是《爱的翅膀》。

1707
01:16:03.060 --> 01:16:05.340
She's accompanied by Dwight on the recorder.
德怀特用竖笛为她伴奏。

1708
01:16:05.960 --> 01:16:07.440
Michael is very moved.
迈克尔非常感动。

1709
01:16:07.560 --> 01:16:08.440
He's holding hands.
他牵着手。

1710
01:16:08.440 --> 01:16:09.300
He's swaying.
他摇晃着身体。

1711
01:16:09.420 --> 01:16:10.340
He's tearing up.
他热泪盈眶。

1712
01:16:10.660 --> 01:16:12.920
We got a lot of questions about this scene.
我们收到了很多关于这场戏的问题。

1713
01:16:13.800 --> 01:16:14.640
Richard H.
理查德·H.

1714
01:16:14.900 --> 01:16:15.960
really covers them all.
真的把这些问题都涵盖了。

1715
01:16:16.240 --> 01:16:19.280
He says, did Rain already know how to play the recorder?
他问，雷恩本来就会吹竖笛吗？

1716
01:16:19.680 --> 01:16:21.860
Did Jenna sing the entire song?
珍娜是唱了整首歌吗？

1717
01:16:22.020 --> 01:16:24.520
Or did the singing end where the scene was cut?
还是说歌声在剪辑点就结束了？

1718
01:16:25.160 --> 01:16:28.140
He also wanted to know, did we rehearse our duet?
他还想知道，我们排练过二重奏吗？

1719
01:16:28.920 --> 01:16:30.280
Here's what I can tell you.
我可以告诉你们这些。

1720
01:16:31.360 --> 01:16:33.460
Yes, Rain knew how to play the recorder.
是的，雷恩会吹竖笛。

1721
01:16:34.200 --> 01:16:36.400
Remember, he played it in Take Your Daughter to Work Day.
别忘了，他在“带女儿上班日”那一集里吹过。

1722
01:16:36.400 --> 01:16:37.940
He was actually very good.
他其实吹得很好。

1723
01:16:38.220 --> 01:16:41.980
But listen to all of the instruments that Rain can play in real life, Angela.
但安吉拉，听听雷恩现实中会玩的乐器吧。

1724
01:16:42.600 --> 01:16:54.100
He can play the recorder, piano, clarinet, saxophone, bassoon, guitar, drums, xylophone, bells, and a little tuba and baritone.
他会吹竖笛、钢琴、单簧管、萨克斯、巴松管、吉他、打鼓、木琴、铃铛，还会一点大号和上低音号。

1725
01:16:54.100 --> 01:16:56.180
What are you, a one-man band, Rain?
你是怎么回事，雷恩，你是单人乐队吗？

1726
01:16:56.620 --> 01:16:57.760
He kind of is.
他确实有点像。

1727
01:16:57.920 --> 01:17:01.660
I knew you could play the bassoon because your book, The Bassoon King, is great.
我知道你会吹巴松管，因为你的书《巴松管之王》很棒。

1728
01:17:01.660 --> 01:17:02.820
So I knew that.
所以我知道这一点。

1729
01:17:03.240 --> 01:17:06.000
But I didn't know you were a walking one-man show.
但我不知道你还是个行走的单人秀。

1730
01:17:06.320 --> 01:17:08.760
Suffice it to say, Rain knew his stuff.
总之，雷恩确实很有料。

1731
01:17:09.460 --> 01:17:13.860
And we did rehearse, but just a little bit right before the scene.
我们确实排练过，但就在拍戏前稍微练了一下。

1732
01:17:14.300 --> 01:17:15.660
Rain and I practiced separately.
雷恩和我分开练习的。

1733
01:17:15.960 --> 01:17:19.000
I had listened to the song over and over again to memorize the words.
我把那首歌听了一遍又一遍，为了记住歌词。

1734
01:17:19.160 --> 01:17:22.640
I had to sing the first verse through the chorus.
我得从第一段唱到副歌。

1735
01:17:23.400 --> 01:17:25.320
That's what I had to do over and over again.
这就是我一遍又一遍练习的内容。

1736
01:17:25.940 --> 01:17:27.380
I was so nervous.
我当时紧张极了。

1737
01:17:28.200 --> 01:17:29.560
Well, I thought you did fantastic.
嗯，我觉得你表现得太棒了。

1738
01:17:30.640 --> 01:17:31.440
Thank you.
谢谢。

1739
01:17:31.680 --> 01:17:33.880
I have a fan question from the scene, Jenna.
珍娜，我这儿有个关于这场戏的粉丝提问。

1740
01:17:34.480 --> 01:17:34.940
Okay.
好的。

1741
01:17:35.500 --> 01:17:40.680
So Chelsea wrote in and said, was Angela's A-man improvised?
切尔西来信问，安吉拉那句“阿门”是即兴发挥的吗？

1742
01:17:40.900 --> 01:17:45.280
A lot of people wrote in about this because it was so quick after Pam is done talking.
很多人都写信问这个问题，因为在帕姆说完话后，那句接得太快了。

1743
01:17:45.440 --> 01:17:47.340
People wanted to know if I improvised that.
大家想知道那是不是我即兴说的。

1744
01:17:47.540 --> 01:17:49.080
No, that was scripted.
不，那是剧本里写的。

1745
01:17:49.660 --> 01:17:52.720
And folks wanted to know why did Angela do it?
大家还想知道安吉拉为什么要那么做？

1746
01:17:52.840 --> 01:17:59.480
And I said, I think personally, the direction that they gave me was that Angela had had enough
我说，我个人认为，导演给我的指示是安吉拉已经受够了

1747
01:17:59.480 --> 01:18:03.340
of this charade, this bird funeral.
这场闹剧，这场鸟的葬礼。

1748
01:18:03.340 --> 01:18:04.940
Pam had gone on and on.
帕姆没完没了地说个不停。

1749
01:18:05.040 --> 01:18:05.300
Enough.
够了。

1750
01:18:05.440 --> 01:18:05.700
Amen.
阿门。

1751
01:18:05.940 --> 01:18:06.640
I'm done.
我搞定了。

1752
01:18:06.880 --> 01:18:09.180
And that's how you finish it.
事情就是这样收尾的。

1753
01:18:09.240 --> 01:18:09.620
Yes.
没错。

1754
01:18:09.900 --> 01:18:10.180
Amen.
阿门。

1755
01:18:10.360 --> 01:18:10.480
Amen.
阿门。

1756
01:18:10.620 --> 01:18:11.060
I'm finished.
我完成了。

1757
01:18:11.280 --> 01:18:11.420
Amen.
阿门。

1758
01:18:11.640 --> 01:18:12.180
Stop talking.
别说了。

1759
01:18:12.880 --> 01:18:13.900
Yes, exactly.
对，没错。

1760
01:18:14.780 --> 01:18:16.880
Speaking of the script, I have a script catch.
说到剧本，我发现了一个剧本上的漏洞。

1761
01:18:17.100 --> 01:18:17.260
Okay.
好的。

1762
01:18:17.500 --> 01:18:19.600
So, you know, in the scene, we set the box on fire.
那个，你知道，在这一幕里，我们把盒子点着了。

1763
01:18:19.840 --> 01:18:22.780
In the shooting draft of the script, we buried the bird.
在拍摄用的剧本草稿里，我们是把那只鸟埋了。

1764
01:18:23.440 --> 01:18:28.420
There was a scene where Michael and Dwight are digging a hole outside and then we all gather
原本有一场戏是迈克尔和德怀特在外面挖坑，然后我们大家都聚在

1765
01:18:28.420 --> 01:18:32.600
around this hole and it got changed to fire, but I don't know why.
这个坑周围，但后来改成了火烧，我不知道为什么。

1766
01:18:32.880 --> 01:18:39.080
I think maybe, Angela, there was really no grass in this area that we shot.
我觉得可能是因为，安吉拉，我们拍摄的那块地方根本没有草。

1767
01:18:39.240 --> 01:18:39.940
We had no grass.
我们那儿没草。

1768
01:18:40.160 --> 01:18:45.060
There was a hedge with maybe like, I don't know, three feet of dirt.
那里只有一道树篱，大概只有三英尺宽的泥地吧。

1769
01:18:45.460 --> 01:18:47.860
Like, yeah, there was, I mean, not even.
对，没错，我是说，甚至连三英尺都没有。

1770
01:18:47.860 --> 01:18:52.960
There is a deleted scene where Michael and Dwight are trying to dig a hole there and then
有一个删减片段是迈克尔和德怀特试图在那里挖坑，然后

1771
01:18:52.960 --> 01:18:55.520
the business on the other side yells at them and they run away.
另一边的商家冲他们大喊大叫，他们就跑开了。

1772
01:18:56.220 --> 01:18:57.600
Oh, okay.
哦，原来如此。

1773
01:18:57.920 --> 01:18:58.840
Well, there you go.
好吧，真相大白了。

1774
01:18:59.380 --> 01:19:02.580
Well, we had another fan question about this fire then.
那我们还有另一个关于这场火的粉丝提问。

1775
01:19:02.920 --> 01:19:06.800
Clara Johnson wants to know, did you actually set the bird on fire?
克拉拉·约翰逊想知道，你们是真的把那只鸟点着了吗？

1776
01:19:07.620 --> 01:19:08.180
Yes.
是的。

1777
01:19:08.360 --> 01:19:09.940
Real fire, fake bird.
真火，假鸟。

1778
01:19:10.160 --> 01:19:15.340
Kent told me they had to hire a special effects guy to oversee the fire and the extinguishing
肯特告诉我，他们必须雇一个特效人员来监督火势和灭火工作，

1779
01:19:15.340 --> 01:19:18.780
and they had to get a special permit to be allowed to set the fire.
而且他们还得申请特别许可才能点火。

1780
01:19:19.000 --> 01:19:22.880
And he said, we did three takes, three takes of the fire.
他说，我们拍了三次，拍了三次火烧的镜头。

1781
01:19:23.080 --> 01:19:28.160
And Phil told me, though, that the special effects guys were worried that the fake dead
不过菲尔告诉我，特效人员担心那只假死

1782
01:19:28.160 --> 01:19:31.200
bird might give off toxic fumes when it burned.
鸟在燃烧时可能会产生有毒烟雾。

1783
01:19:31.280 --> 01:19:35.840
So we, they actually took it out of the box and just put a wad of toilet paper in there.
所以我们，他们实际上把它从盒子里拿了出来，只放了一团卫生纸进去。

1784
01:19:36.180 --> 01:19:38.120
Oh, not toilet paper.
哦，不是卫生纸吧。

1785
01:19:39.020 --> 01:19:39.960
I know.
我知道。

1786
01:19:40.640 --> 01:19:41.240
Too soon.
太早了。

1787
01:19:41.320 --> 01:19:41.370
I know.
我知道。

1788
01:19:41.580 --> 01:19:42.400
Too soon, Angela.
太早了，安吉拉。

1789
01:19:42.760 --> 01:19:43.180
Too soon.
太早了。

1790
01:19:44.700 --> 01:19:49.200
And then finally, we had a fan catch from Peter Kay.
最后，我们收到了彼得·凯的一个粉丝发现。

1791
01:19:49.580 --> 01:19:53.200
He said, I noticed the box was burned in some shredded paper.
他说，我注意到盒子里烧的是一些碎纸。

1792
01:19:53.760 --> 01:19:57.080
Could this be further evidence that Pam does use the shredder?
这是否能进一步证明帕姆确实会用碎纸机？

1793
01:19:57.480 --> 01:19:59.140
Oh, look at that.
哦，看看这个。

1794
01:19:59.560 --> 01:20:00.620
Nice one, Peter.
干得好，彼得。

1795
01:20:00.960 --> 01:20:02.100
It would appear so.
看起来确实如此。

1796
01:20:02.500 --> 01:20:07.060
Well, you know, Jen actually left us a really great message about this scene.
嗯，你知道，简其实给我们留了一条关于这场戏的很棒的信息。

1797
01:20:07.060 --> 01:20:12.400
And she was talking about the fact that we never got to shoot outside.
她谈到了我们从未有机会在户外拍摄的事实。

1798
01:20:12.400 --> 01:20:15.400
And when we did, everyone would get really excited.
而当我们真的去户外拍摄时，每个人都会非常兴奋。

1799
01:20:15.740 --> 01:20:18.040
And she explains a little bit about that.
她对此做了一些解释。

1800
01:20:18.240 --> 01:20:19.640
So, Sam, can you play that?
所以，萨姆，你能播放一下吗？

1801
01:20:20.040 --> 01:20:26.120
One thing that I remember from the grief counseling episode is that when I went to the sound mix,
关于“悲伤辅导”那一集，我记得有一件事，当时我去参加混音制作时，

1802
01:20:26.320 --> 01:20:28.680
they were showing us the playback of the episode.
他们正在给我们播放那一集的样片。

1803
01:20:29.360 --> 01:20:32.480
And it was still a little bit unusual when the characters went outside.
当角色们走到户外时，感觉还是有点不寻常。

1804
01:20:32.540 --> 01:20:34.180
It was still a little bit of a treat.
那依然算是一种小小的享受。

1805
01:20:34.180 --> 01:20:41.480
So, we get to this bird funeral scene, and our characters are outside.
所以，当我们看到那场鸟儿葬礼的戏时，角色们都在户外。

1806
01:20:41.560 --> 01:20:47.840
And I just remember hearing kind of an enormous amount of birds.
我只记得当时听到了极其大量的鸟叫声。

1807
01:20:47.840 --> 01:20:52.240
And I think that it was because we were outside.
我想那是因为我们在户外。

1808
01:20:52.240 --> 01:20:54.300
It was because we had a bird funeral.
是因为我们在举行一场鸟儿葬礼。

1809
01:20:55.300 --> 01:21:04.120
It was so exciting for the amazing sound people, who do a fantastic job, to put a lot of bird noises in.
对于那些出色的音效师来说，能加入大量的鸟叫声一定让他们感到非常兴奋，他们做得太棒了。

1810
01:21:04.220 --> 01:21:10.460
Because for the longest time, when we're inside the office, they're just putting dot-matric printer sounds
因为在很长一段时间里，当我们待在办公室里时，他们只能加入针式打印机的声音，

1811
01:21:10.460 --> 01:21:15.180
and just faxes and old-fashioned office noises.
还有传真机和老式办公室的噪音。

1812
01:21:15.280 --> 01:21:21.420
So, it must have been such a treat and a field day to be able to go outside and hear birds,
所以，能去户外听到鸟叫声，对他们来说一定是一种享受，简直像过节一样，

1813
01:21:21.420 --> 01:21:23.720
and especially on theme with the funeral.
尤其是还契合葬礼的主题。

1814
01:21:24.000 --> 01:21:29.740
So, I remember, it was a slight exaggeration, but it sounded a little bit like Alfred Hitchcock,
所以，我记得当时稍微有点夸张，听起来有点像阿尔弗雷德·希区柯克的电影，

1815
01:21:29.820 --> 01:21:34.500
the birds, when I first heard the playback for the bird funeral.
我第一次听到鸟儿葬礼的样片时，那些鸟叫声就是这种感觉。

1816
01:21:34.740 --> 01:21:40.520
But they quickly made a wonderful adjustment, and it was the right amount of outside birds.
但他们很快做出了很棒的调整，调整到了恰到好处的户外鸟叫声量。

1817
01:21:41.840 --> 01:21:42.780
I love that.
我喜欢这一点。

1818
01:21:42.880 --> 01:21:45.140
I love that our sound mixers got so excited.
我喜欢我们的音效师们如此兴奋的样子。

1819
01:21:45.280 --> 01:21:47.260
They put, like, hundreds of birds, and they were like,
他们加了成百上千只鸟，然后他们说，

1820
01:21:47.260 --> 01:21:50.220
Okay, guys, there's not this many birds outside.
“好吧，伙计们，外面没这么多鸟。”

1821
01:21:50.540 --> 01:21:52.200
Let's dial it back.
“我们调小一点吧。”

1822
01:21:53.140 --> 01:21:54.340
Yes, yes.
没错，没错。

1823
01:21:54.840 --> 01:21:58.200
Oh, what good insight from Jen this week.
哦，Jen这周的见解真好。

